<subpara id="X36100000I7009J_11" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X36100000I7009J_12" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="X36100000I7009J_12_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000BK100000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (4 Wheel Drive Control Switch - 4WD Computer Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000068800EX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the 4WD computer assembly connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C117072J13" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the 4WD computer assembly and body ground. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
</test1>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<spec>
<table>
<title>Resistance:</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2 (4WDS) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Switch ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 Ω or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2 (4WDS) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Switch OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X36100000I7009J_12_0005" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X36100000I7009J_12_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X36100000I7009J_12_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000BK200000">
<testtitle>Inspect 4 Wheel Drive Control Switch</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the 4 wheel drive control switch connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C134829J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the 4 wheel drive control switch.</ptxt>
</test1>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<spec>
<table>
<title>Resistance:</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4(B) - 1(GND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Switch ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 Ω or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4(B) - 1(GND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Switch OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<test1>
<ptxt>Illumination Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Connect the battery positive (+) to terminal 3 (ILL+) and the negative (-) to terminal 2 (ILL-) of the 4 wheel drive control switch, and check that the illumination comes on.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Comes on</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X36100000I7009J_12_0004" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X36100000I7009J_12_0003" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
